{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-04T16:30:51.567Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"bed13a5c835cb1797604de67","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-rl-hjg1"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Persisted bounded recursive self-improvement loop (pm rl loop run)"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Execute the collect -> train -> evaluate -> compare -> promote-or-reject cycle as a persisted pm-rl command: every generation records a collection Run with merge-safe metric notes and a Generation item, promotion goes through the existing transactional, budget-checked gate, refusal reasons are recorded as item history, and evaluation results deterministically derive the next generation's training and evaluation configuration. Hard bounds: max generations, total sample budget, regression guard, no promotion without a strictly better held-out evaluation. Uses the deterministic built-in contextual bandit as the trainer so the loop runs end to end in tests and a manual CLI demo."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["execution","recursive-training","roadmap"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-04T16:30:51.567Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-04T16:30:51.567Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"pi-glm"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":480},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"pm rl loop run executes a bounded multi-generation loop end to end against a real tracker and promotes only via the existing transactional promotion flow; Each generation leaves a collection Run item with per-sample metric notes and a Generation item; refusal reasons are recorded in item history; The next generation's learning rate and evaluation sample count are derived deterministically from the previous evaluation results; Generation limit, sample budget, unchanged checkpoint, widening gap, statistical gate refusal and approval budget exhaustion all stop the loop with a distinct recorded reason; Two loops run concurrently on two real Git branches merge losslessly: all items and metric notes survive in both directions"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-rl-apvf"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"d5974e8f81bac72cca8a64935e282ea53135fe0b870a967c44d38eb1015bbffb","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"02621022ec77842b56e60b5d8ba38f8f982bb1e9ec7f35d246e7c9c1e0feb5db"}
